---
import SimLayout from '../../../layouts/SimLayout.astro';
---

<SimLayout
  areaSlug="electronics"
  title="Capacitor"
  description="Every charge is a ball you can count. Drive the source by hand and watch electrons get dragged off one plate, all the way around the circuit, onto the other one, until the field they build pushes back exactly as hard as you are pushing."
>
  <div class="sim">
    <div class="sim-stage">
      <canvas id="cp" class="cp-canvas" width="1000" height="880"></canvas>
    </div>

    <div class="sim-panel">
      <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap">
        <button class="btn" id="run">Pause</button>
        <button class="btn ghost" id="reset">Reset</button>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Source</label>
        <div class="seg" id="src">
          <button data-s="manual" class="active">Manual</button>
          <button data-s="dc">Battery</button>
          <button data-s="ac">AC</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="control" id="ctl-v">
        <label><span id="vlab">Drive it yourself</span> <b id="vsval">0.0 V</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="vs" min="-120" max="120" step="1" value="0" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span id="vhint">drag me up and down</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control" id="ctl-sw">
        <label>Switch</label>
        <div class="seg" id="mode">
          <button data-m="charge" class="active">Charge</button>
          <button data-m="discharge">Discharge</button>
          <button data-m="auto">Auto</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="control" id="ctl-f">
        <label>Frequency <b id="fval">—</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="freq" min="5" max="200" step="5" value="15" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>slow</span><span>fast</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Resistor R <b id="rval">10 kΩ</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="r" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="50" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>100 Ω</span><span>1 MΩ</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Plate area A <b id="aval">1.00 m²</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="a" min="10" max="200" step="2" value="100" />
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Plate gap d <b id="dval">10 µm</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="d" min="1" max="50" step="1" value="10" />
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Dielectric κ <b id="kval">1.0</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="k" min="10" max="120" step="1" value="10" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>vacuum</span><span>ceramic</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Time rate <b id="rateval">1.0×</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="rate" min="10" max="300" step="5" value="100" />
      </div>

      <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="lines" checked /> Draw a field line for every pair</label>

      <div class="readout">
        <div class="row"><span id="l1">Charge on the plates</span><b id="r1">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l2">Voltage across</span><b id="r2">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l3">Current</span><b id="r3">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l4">Capacitance</span><b id="r4">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l5">Time constant</span><b id="r5">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l6">Field between plates</span><b id="r6">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l7">Energy stored</span><b id="r7">—</b></div>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:var(--text-faint);margin:0;line-height:1.5">
        Each ball is a real packet of charge, and the number sitting on the
        plates is exactly Q divided by that packet. One field line is drawn per
        pair.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="observe">
    <li>
      Start in Manual and push the slider up slowly. Electrons are dragged off
      the top plate, travel the long way round through the wire, and land on the
      bottom one. <b>Nothing crosses the gap.</b> The top plate is positive only
      because it is missing exactly as many electrons as the bottom plate gained.
    </li>
    <li>
      Watch the whole line of electrons in the wire, not just one of them. They
      all creep forward together, and a ball lands on the plate at one end while
      another leaves at the far end in the same instant. Real drift is
      millimetres per second: charge appears at the plate immediately not
      because an electron raced there, but because the entire queue shifted.
    </li>
    <li>
      Now hold the slider still at any value. The balls stop dead. <b>Current
      flows only while the charge is changing</b>, which is the whole of
      I = C dV/dt in one picture. Jerk the slider and watch the current spike,
      move it gently and barely anything happens.
    </li>
    <li>
      Look at the two markers on the voltage ladder. The current is set by the
      <b>gap between them</b>, not by either one alone. As the capacitor catches
      up with the source that gap closes and the flow dies, which is exactly why
      charging tails off instead of stopping abruptly.
    </li>
    <li>
      Count the field lines. Every one starts on a positive ball and ends on a
      negative ball, so the field between the plates is a picture of the charge,
      and the voltage is that field times the gap. Squeeze the gap and the same
      charge now means less voltage: that is what more capacitance is.
    </li>
    <li>
      Push the slider negative. The balls drain off, cross zero, and pile up on
      the other side with the field lines reversing with them. A capacitor has no
      preferred direction, it only ever holds a difference.
    </li>
    <li>
      Switch to AC and start slow. The charge sloshes back and forth, the same
      electrons going nowhere on average, and yet a current flows all cycle. Now
      raise the frequency: the plates end up less charged each cycle, and the
      current gets <b>bigger</b>, because current is charge per unit time and the
      sloshing got faster.
    </li>
    <li>
      In AC, watch when the current peaks. It is largest as the voltage crosses
      zero and vanishes at the peaks of the voltage, a quarter cycle out of step.
      The current <b>leads</b>, and that is why a capacitor blocks DC and passes
      high frequencies.
    </li>
  </Fragment>
</SimLayout>

<script>
  import { setupCanvas, makeText, subHtml } from '../../../lib/sim';

  const EPS0 = 8.854e-12;

  const state = {
    src: 'manual' as 'manual' | 'dc' | 'ac',
    mode: 'charge' as 'charge' | 'discharge' | 'auto',
    vs: 0, // slider volts: live drive, battery voltage, or AC amplitude
    freq: 0.15, // in units of 1/τ, so the interesting range is always reachable
    r: 10000,
    area: 1.0,
    d: 10e-6,
    kappa: 1,
    rate: 1,
    running: true,
    lines: true,
  };

  const VMAX = 12; // what the slider can reach, used to size the charge packet

  let v = 0; // capacitor voltage
  let t = 0; // simulated seconds since the last switch flip
  let tAC = 0; // AC phase clock
  let phase: 'charge' | 'discharge' = 'charge';
  let train = 0; // how far the queue of electrons has crept, in pixels
  let wBatt = 0, wRes = 0;
  let hist: { t: number; vs: number; v: number; i: number }[] = [];
  let histT = 0;
  let clock = 0;

  const cap = () => (EPS0 * state.kappa * state.area) / state.d;
  const tau = () => cap() * state.r;
  /** Cycles per second, tied to τ so the useful range is always on the dial. */
  const freqHz = () => state.freq / tau();

  function vSource() {
    if (state.src === 'manual') return state.vs;
    if (state.src === 'ac') return state.vs * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * freqHz() * tAC);
    return phase === 'charge' ? state.vs : 0;
  }
  const current = () => (vSource() - v) / state.r;

  /** One ball is this much charge, sized so a full swing shows about 20. */
  const qBall = () => (cap() * VMAX) / 20;

  function reset() {
    v = 0;
    t = 0;
    tAC = 0;
    train = 0;
    wBatt = wRes = 0;
    hist = [];
    histT = 0;
    pops = [];
    lastN = 0;
    phase = state.mode === 'discharge' ? 'discharge' : 'charge';
    if (state.src === 'dc' && phase === 'discharge') v = state.vs;
  }

  function physics(dtReal: number) {
    // One time constant takes about a second on screen, whatever R and C are.
    const dt = dtReal * state.rate * (tau() / 0.9);
    const steps = 10;
    const h = dt / steps;
    for (let s = 0; s < steps; s++) {
      tAC += h;
      const i = current();
      wBatt += vSource() * i * h;
      wRes += i * i * state.r * h;
      v += (i / cap()) * h;
    }
    t += dt;
    histT += dt;
    hist.push({ t: histT, vs: vSource(), v, i: current() });
    const span = 10 * tau();
    while (hist.length > 2 && hist[0].t < histT - span) hist.shift();
    if (state.src === 'dc' && state.mode === 'auto' && t > 5 * tau()) {
      phase = phase === 'charge' ? 'discharge' : 'charge';
      t = 0;
    }
  }

  // --- formatting ------------------------------------------------------------

  function eng(x: number, unit: string, digits = 2): string {
    const a = Math.abs(x);
    if (a === 0) return `0 ${unit}`;
    const steps: [number, string][] = [
      [1e-15, 'f'], [1e-12, 'p'], [1e-9, 'n'], [1e-6, 'µ'], [1e-3, 'm'],
      [1, ''], [1e3, 'k'], [1e6, 'M'], [1e9, 'G'],
    ];
    let pick = steps[0];
    for (const s of steps) if (a >= s[0]) pick = s;
    return `${(x / pick[0]).toFixed(digits)} ${pick[1]}${unit}`;
  }
  const fmtR = (r: number) =>
    r >= 1e6 ? (r / 1e6).toFixed(r >= 1e7 ? 0 : 1) + ' MΩ'
    : r >= 1000 ? (r / 1000).toFixed(r >= 1e4 ? 0 : 1) + ' kΩ'
    : r.toFixed(0) + ' Ω';

  // --- canvas ----------------------------------------------------------------

  const canvas = document.getElementById('cp') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const { ctx, W, H } = setupCanvas(canvas, () => draw());
  const cssVar = (n: string) => getComputedStyle(canvas).getPropertyValue(n).trim();
  const inkRGB = () => cssVar('--stage-ink') || '232,233,236';
  const inkA = (a: number) => `rgba(${inkRGB()},${a})`;
  const bg = () => cssVar('--stage-bg') || '#0d0e12';
  const { label, textWidth } = makeText(ctx, inkA);

  const NEG = '#5b8cff'; // electrons
  const POS = '#f9736a'; // the holes they left behind
  const ACC = '#7c8cff';
  const WARM = '#f59e0b';
  const GREEN = '#34d399';

  const SCENE = { x: 20, y: 76, w: 960, h: 560 };
  const SCOPE = { x: 20, y: 668, w: 620, h: 192 };
  const SIDE = { x: 660, y: 668, w: 320, h: 192 };

  function rr(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, r: number) {
    const rad = Math.min(r, Math.abs(w) / 2, Math.abs(h) / 2);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x + rad, y);
    ctx.lineTo(x + w - rad, y);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x + w, y, x + w, y + rad);
    ctx.lineTo(x + w, y + h - rad);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x + w, y + h, x + w - rad, y + h);
    ctx.lineTo(x + rad, y + h);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x, y + h, x, y + h - rad);
    ctx.lineTo(x, y + rad);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x, y, x + rad, y);
    ctx.closePath();
  }
  function panel(p: { x: number; y: number; w: number; h: number }, title: string) {
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.1);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    rr(p.x, p.y, p.w, p.h, 10);
    ctx.stroke();
    label(title, p.x + 2, p.y - 9, 0.5, 'left', 11);
  }
  function arrow(x1: number, y1: number, x2: number, y2: number, size = 5) {
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x1, y1);
    ctx.lineTo(x2, y2);
    ctx.stroke();
    const a = Math.atan2(y2 - y1, x2 - x1);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x2, y2);
    ctx.lineTo(x2 - size * Math.cos(a - 0.4), y2 - size * Math.sin(a - 0.4));
    ctx.lineTo(x2 - size * Math.cos(a + 0.4), y2 - size * Math.sin(a + 0.4));
    ctx.closePath();
    ctx.fill();
  }

  // --- geometry --------------------------------------------------------------

  type Pt = { x: number; y: number };

  function geom() {
    const cy = SCENE.y + 300;
    const pw = 250 + (state.area / 2) * 200; // area stretches the plates
    const gapPx = 74 + (state.d / 50e-6) * 150; // and d opens the gap
    const cx = SCENE.x + 540;
    const th = 20;
    const topY = cy - gapPx / 2 - th;
    const botY = cy + gapPx / 2;
    return { cx, cy, pw, gapPx, th, topY, botY, x0: cx - pw / 2, x1: cx + pw / 2 };
  }

  /**
   * The road the electrons take: off the top plate, up, around the left where
   * the source is, and back onto the bottom plate. It deliberately does not
   * cross the gap, because charge never does.
   */
  function wirePath(): Pt[] {
    const g = geom();
    const yTop = SCENE.y + 58, yBot = SCENE.y + SCENE.h - 58, xLeft = SCENE.x + 120;
    return [
      { x: g.cx, y: g.topY },
      { x: g.cx, y: yTop },
      { x: xLeft, y: yTop },
      { x: xLeft, y: yBot },
      { x: g.cx, y: yBot },
      { x: g.cx, y: g.botY + g.th },
    ];
  }

  function pathLength(p: Pt[]) {
    let L = 0;
    for (let k = 1; k < p.length; k++) L += Math.hypot(p[k].x - p[k - 1].x, p[k].y - p[k - 1].y);
    return L;
  }
  function pointAt(p: Pt[], d: number): Pt {
    let rem = Math.max(0, d);
    for (let k = 1; k < p.length; k++) {
      const seg = Math.hypot(p[k].x - p[k - 1].x, p[k].y - p[k - 1].y);
      if (rem <= seg) {
        const f = seg === 0 ? 0 : rem / seg;
        return { x: p[k - 1].x + (p[k].x - p[k - 1].x) * f, y: p[k - 1].y + (p[k].y - p[k - 1].y) * f };
      }
      rem -= seg;
    }
    return p[p.length - 1];
  }
  function strokePath(p: Pt[], alpha = 0.4) {
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(alpha);
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(p[0].x, p[0].y);
    for (let k = 1; k < p.length; k++) ctx.lineTo(p[k].x, p[k].y);
    ctx.stroke();
  }

  // --- the charges -----------------------------------------------------------

  const BALL = 6.4;
  const SPACING = 34; // how far apart the electrons sit in the wire

  function drawBall(x: number, y: number, negative: boolean, alpha = 1) {
    ctx.globalAlpha = alpha;
    ctx.fillStyle = negative ? NEG : POS;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(x, y, BALL, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();
    ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(255,255,255,0.55)';
    ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x - 3, y);
    ctx.lineTo(x + 3, y);
    if (!negative) {
      ctx.moveTo(x, y - 3);
      ctx.lineTo(x, y + 3);
    }
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
  }

  /** Where the k-th ball sits along a plate face. */
  function ballSlot(g: ReturnType<typeof geom>, k: number, n: number, top: boolean) {
    const perRow = Math.max(1, Math.floor((g.pw - 26) / 27));
    const row = Math.floor(k / perRow);
    const inRow = k % perRow;
    const count = Math.min(perRow, n - row * perRow);
    const x = g.x0 + 16 + ((inRow + 0.5) * (g.pw - 32)) / Math.max(1, count);
    const y = top ? g.topY + g.th + 13 + row * 17 : g.botY - 13 - row * 17;
    return { x, y };
  }

  type Pop = { x: number; y: number; life: number; neg: boolean };
  let pops: Pop[] = [];
  let lastN = 0;

  function drawCharges() {
    const g = geom();
    const q = cap() * v;
    const n = Math.min(40, Math.floor(Math.abs(q) / qBall()));
    const topPositive = q >= 0;

    // every time the count ticks up, both ends get a landing
    if (n > lastN && n <= 40) {
      const a = ballSlot(g, n - 1, n, true), b = ballSlot(g, n - 1, n, false);
      pops.push({ x: a.x, y: a.y, life: 1, neg: !topPositive });
      pops.push({ x: b.x, y: b.y, life: 1, neg: topPositive });
      if (pops.length > 24) pops.splice(0, pops.length - 24);
    }
    lastN = n;

    // one field line per pair of charges, starting on the positive ball
    if (state.lines && n > 0) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(245,158,11,${0.25 + 0.4 * Math.min(1, n / 14)})`;
      ctx.fillStyle = ctx.strokeStyle;
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.3;
      for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) {
        const a = ballSlot(g, k, n, true), b = ballSlot(g, k, n, false);
        if (topPositive) arrow(a.x, a.y + 10, b.x, b.y - 10, 5);
        else arrow(b.x, b.y - 10, a.x, a.y + 10, 5);
      }
    }

    // the plates themselves
    ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.3);
    rr(g.x0, g.topY, g.pw, g.th, 4);
    ctx.fill();
    rr(g.x0, g.botY, g.pw, g.th, 4);
    ctx.fill();

    for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) {
      const a = ballSlot(g, k, n, true), b = ballSlot(g, k, n, false);
      drawBall(a.x, a.y, !topPositive);
      drawBall(b.x, b.y, topPositive);
    }

    for (const p of pops) {
      const a = Math.max(0, p.life);
      ctx.strokeStyle = p.neg ? `rgba(91,140,255,${a * 0.8})` : `rgba(249,115,106,${a * 0.8})`;
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(p.x, p.y, BALL + (1 - a) * 14, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.stroke();
    }

    // the queue of electrons in the wire, all creeping along together
    const path = wirePath();
    const L = pathLength(path);
    const off = ((train % SPACING) + SPACING) % SPACING;
    for (let s = off; s < L; s += SPACING) {
      const p = pointAt(path, s);
      drawBall(p.x, p.y, true, 0.95);
    }
    return { n, q };
  }

  // --- the source ------------------------------------------------------------

  function drawSource(x: number, y: number) {
    const vsrc = vSource();
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    if (state.src === 'ac') {
      ctx.fillStyle = bg();
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(x, y, 28, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.6);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.beginPath();
      for (let k = 0; k <= 24; k++) {
        const f = k / 24;
        const px = x - 16 + f * 32;
        const py = y - Math.sin(f * Math.PI * 2) * 10;
        k ? ctx.lineTo(px, py) : ctx.moveTo(px, py);
      }
      ctx.stroke();
    } else if (state.src === 'manual') {
      // a knob you are turning: the pointer follows the slider
      ctx.fillStyle = bg();
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(x, y, 30, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.5);
      ctx.stroke();
      const ang = -Math.PI / 2 + (vsrc / VMAX) * 2.2;
      ctx.strokeStyle = ACC;
      ctx.lineWidth = 3;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(x, y);
      ctx.lineTo(x + Math.cos(ang) * 22, y + Math.sin(ang) * 22);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.fillStyle = ACC;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(x, y, 3.6, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
    } else {
      ctx.fillStyle = bg();
      ctx.fillRect(x - 24, y - 22, 48, 44);
      for (let k = 0; k < 2; k++) {
        const yy = y - 8 + k * 16;
        const half = k === 0 ? 17 : 9;
        ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.6);
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.moveTo(x - half, yy);
        ctx.lineTo(x + half, yy);
        ctx.stroke();
      }
      // the switch, thrown open while discharging
      ctx.fillStyle = bg();
      ctx.fillRect(x - 20, y - 60, 46, 30);
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.6);
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(x, y - 56);
      if (phase === 'charge') ctx.lineTo(x, y - 30);
      else ctx.lineTo(x + 19, y - 40);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.6);
      for (const yy of [y - 56, y - 30]) {
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(x, yy, 3, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.fill();
      }
    }
    label(`${vsrc >= 0 ? '+' : ''}${vsrc.toFixed(2)} V`, x + 42, y - 4, 0.85, 'left', 14, WARM);
    label(
      state.src === 'manual' ? 'you, driving it' : state.src === 'ac' ? 'AC source' : 'battery',
      x + 42,
      y + 14,
      0.45,
      'left',
      11
    );
  }

  function drawResistor(x: number, y: number, len: number) {
    ctx.fillStyle = bg();
    ctx.fillRect(x - 2, y - 13, len + 4, 26);
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.6);
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.beginPath();
    const n = 6, amp = 9;
    ctx.moveTo(x, y);
    for (let k = 0; k <= n; k++) ctx.lineTo(x + ((k + 0.5) * len) / (n + 1), y + (k % 2 ? amp : -amp));
    ctx.lineTo(x + len, y);
    ctx.stroke();
    label(fmtR(state.r), x + len / 2, y - 20, 0.55, 'center', 12);
  }

  // --- the voltage ladder ----------------------------------------------------

  /** Two markers and the gap between them, which is what drives the current. */
  function drawLadder() {
    const x = SCENE.x + SCENE.w - 96;
    const top = SCENE.y + 78, bot = SCENE.y + SCENE.h - 96;
    const mid = (top + bot) / 2;
    const Y = (vv: number) => mid - (Math.max(-VMAX, Math.min(VMAX, vv)) / VMAX) * ((bot - top) / 2);

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.22);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x, top);
    ctx.lineTo(x, bot);
    ctx.stroke();
    for (let vv = -12; vv <= 12; vv += 3) {
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(x - 5, Y(vv));
      ctx.lineTo(x + 5, Y(vv));
      ctx.stroke();
      if (vv % 6 === 0) label(`${vv}`, x - 9, Y(vv) + 4, 0.35, 'right', 10);
    }

    const vsrc = vSource();
    // the difference: this is the whole reason a current exists
    ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(245,158,11,0.25)';
    ctx.fillRect(x - 7, Math.min(Y(vsrc), Y(v)), 14, Math.abs(Y(vsrc) - Y(v)));

    const drawn: number[] = [];
    for (const [vv, col, name] of [
      [vsrc, WARM, 'source'],
      [v, ACC, 'capacitor'],
    ] as [number, string, string][]) {
      ctx.fillStyle = col;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(x + 7, Y(vv));
      ctx.lineTo(x + 20, Y(vv) - 7);
      ctx.lineTo(x + 20, Y(vv) + 7);
      ctx.closePath();
      ctx.fill();
      // when the two markers land on top of each other, stack the labels
      const clash = drawn.some((yy) => Math.abs(yy - Y(vv)) < 15);
      label(name, x + 25, Y(vv) + (clash ? 17 : 4), 0.8, 'left', 11, col);
      drawn.push(Y(vv));
    }
    label('volts', x, top - 14, 0.45, 'center', 11);
    const dv = vsrc - v;
    label(`difference ${dv >= 0 ? '+' : ''}${dv.toFixed(2)} V`, x - 4, bot + 24, 0.7, 'center', 12, WARM);
    label('this is what pushes the current', x - 4, bot + 42, 0.4, 'center', 10);
  }

  // --- the scene -------------------------------------------------------------

  function drawScene() {
    panel(SCENE, 'INSIDE THE CIRCUIT');
    const g = geom();
    const path = wirePath();
    strokePath(path);

    const yTop = SCENE.y + 58, xLeft = SCENE.x + 120;
    drawResistor(xLeft + 130, yTop, 140);
    drawSource(xLeft, g.cy);

    const { n, q } = drawCharges();

    label(
      q >= 0 ? 'electrons missing here' : 'extra electrons here',
      g.x0 - 14,
      g.topY + 4,
      0.6,
      'right',
      12,
      q >= 0 ? POS : NEG
    );
    label(
      q >= 0 ? 'and they all ended up here' : 'dragged off from here',
      g.x0 - 14,
      g.botY + g.th - 2,
      0.6,
      'right',
      12,
      q >= 0 ? NEG : POS
    );

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.3);
    ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.3);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    const dx = g.x1 + 16;
    arrow(dx, g.topY + g.th, dx, g.botY, 5);
    arrow(dx, g.botY, dx, g.topY + g.th, 5);
    label(`d = ${(state.d * 1e6).toFixed(0)} µm`, dx + 8, g.cy - 4, 0.5, 'left', 11);
    label(`E = ${eng(v / state.d, 'V/m', 0)}`, dx + 8, g.cy + 14, 0.5, 'left', 11, WARM);

    label(
      `${n} pair${n === 1 ? '' : 's'} on the plates  ·  one ball = ${eng(qBall(), 'C', 1)}`,
      SCENE.x + SCENE.w - 20,
      SCENE.y + SCENE.h - 18,
      0.55,
      'right',
      12
    );
    label(`Q = ${eng(q, 'C')}`, g.cx, SCENE.y + 32, 0.85, 'center', 14, q >= 0 ? POS : NEG);

    // the current, shown where it happens: on the wire, pointing the way the
    // electrons are actually creeping
    const i = current();
    const yBot = SCENE.y + SCENE.h - 58;
    const moving = Math.abs(i) > 1e-13;
    if (moving) {
      const dir = i > 0 ? 1 : -1; // conventional current one way, electrons the other
      ctx.strokeStyle = GREEN;
      ctx.fillStyle = GREEN;
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      const mx = (xLeft + g.cx) / 2;
      arrow(mx - dir * 34, yBot + 26, mx + dir * 34, yBot + 26, 8);
      label(`electrons: ${eng(Math.abs(i), 'A')}`, mx, yBot + 48, 0.8, 'center', 12, GREEN);
    } else {
      label('nothing is moving', (xLeft + g.cx) / 2, yBot + 30, 0.5, 'center', 12);
      label('the charge is not changing', (xLeft + g.cx) / 2, yBot + 48, 0.4, 'center', 10);
    }
    drawLadder();
  }

  // --- scope -----------------------------------------------------------------

  function drawScope() {
    panel(SCOPE, 'WHAT THE SOURCE DOES, AND WHAT THE CHARGE DOES');
    const px = SCOPE.x + 58, py = SCOPE.y + 22, pw = SCOPE.w - 78, ph = SCOPE.h - 58;
    const span = 10 * tau();
    const t1 = Math.max(span, histT), t0 = t1 - span;
    const X = (tt: number) => px + ((tt - t0) / span) * pw;
    let vmax = 0.5;
    for (const h of hist) vmax = Math.max(vmax, Math.abs(h.vs), Math.abs(h.v));
    const Yv = (vv: number) => py + ph * 0.4 - (vv / vmax) * (ph * 0.34);
    let imax = 1e-15;
    for (const h of hist) imax = Math.max(imax, Math.abs(h.i));
    const Yi = (ii: number) => py + ph * 0.85 - (ii / imax) * (ph * 0.13);

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.18);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, py);
    ctx.lineTo(px, py + ph);
    ctx.lineTo(px + pw, py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();
    for (const [y, txt] of [
      [Yv(0), '0 V'],
      [Yi(0), '0 A'],
    ] as [number, string][]) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.12);
      ctx.setLineDash([3, 3]);
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(px, y);
      ctx.lineTo(px + pw, y);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.setLineDash([]);
      label(txt, px - 6, y + 4, 0.35, 'right', 10);
    }
    label(`${vmax.toFixed(1)} V`, px - 6, Yv(vmax) + 4, 0.35, 'right', 10);

    if (hist.length > 1) {
      const series: [string, (h: (typeof hist)[0]) => number, number][] = [
        [WARM, (h) => Yv(h.vs), 1.6],
        [ACC, (h) => Yv(h.v), 2.2],
        [GREEN, (h) => Yi(h.i), 1.8],
      ];
      for (const [col, fn, lw] of series) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = col;
        ctx.lineWidth = lw;
        ctx.beginPath();
        hist.forEach((h, k) => (k ? ctx.lineTo(X(h.t), fn(h)) : ctx.moveTo(X(h.t), fn(h))));
        ctx.stroke();
      }
    }
    label('current', px + pw, py + 12, 0.85, 'right', 11, GREEN);
    label('capacitor', px + pw - 62, py + 12, 0.85, 'right', 11, ACC);
    label('source', px + pw - 152, py + 12, 0.85, 'right', 11, WARM);
    label(`window = 10 τ = ${eng(10 * tau(), 's')}`, px + pw, py + ph + 18, 0.4, 'right', 10);
  }

  // --- side panel: phasors in AC, energy otherwise ---------------------------

  function drawSide() {
    if (state.src === 'ac') {
      panel(SIDE, 'WHO LEADS WHOM');
      const cx = SIDE.x + SIDE.w / 2, cy = SIDE.y + 62, rad = 40;
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.14);
      ctx.lineWidth = 1;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(cx, cy, rad, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.stroke();
      const w = 2 * Math.PI * freqHz();
      const xc = 1 / (w * cap());
      const theta = Math.atan2(xc, state.r); // how far the current leads
      const ang = -2 * Math.PI * freqHz() * tAC;
      const arms: [number, number, string, string][] = [
        [ang, 1, WARM, 'source'],
        [ang + theta, 0.9, GREEN, 'I'],
        [ang + theta - Math.PI / 2, Math.max(0.15, xc / Math.hypot(state.r, xc)), ACC, 'V_C'],
      ];
      for (const [a, len, col] of arms) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = col;
        ctx.fillStyle = col;
        ctx.lineWidth = 2.2;
        arrow(cx, cy, cx + Math.cos(a) * rad * len, cy + Math.sin(a) * rad * len, 7);
      }
      // a fixed key, so nothing chases the spinning arrows around
      let lx = SIDE.x + 22;
      for (const [, , col, name] of arms) {
        ctx.fillStyle = col;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(lx, cy + rad + 16, 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.fill();
        label(name, lx + 9, cy + rad + 20, 0.7, 'left', 10, col);
        lx += textWidth(name, 10) + 34;
      }
      label(
        `current leads by ${((theta * 180) / Math.PI).toFixed(0)}°`,
        SIDE.x + SIDE.w / 2,
        SIDE.y + SIDE.h - 42,
        0.75,
        'center',
        12,
        GREEN
      );
      label(`X_C = 1/2πfC = ${fmtR(xc)}`, SIDE.x + SIDE.w / 2, SIDE.y + SIDE.h - 24, 0.55, 'center', 11);
      label(`at ${eng(freqHz(), 'Hz', 1)}`, SIDE.x + SIDE.w / 2, SIDE.y + SIDE.h - 8, 0.4, 'center', 10);
      return;
    }
    panel(SIDE, 'WHERE THE ENERGY WENT');
    const u = 0.5 * cap() * v * v;
    const top = SIDE.y + 34, x0 = SIDE.x + 92, bw = SIDE.w - 116;
    const scale = Math.max(1e-18, Math.abs(wBatt), u + wRes);
    const bars: [string, number, string][] = [
      ['source', wBatt, inkA(0.35)],
      ['stored', u, ACC],
      ['heat in R', wRes, WARM],
    ];
    bars.forEach(([name, val, col], k) => {
      const y = top + k * 34;
      label(name, x0 - 10, y + 13, 0.55, 'right', 11);
      ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.07);
      rr(x0, y, bw, 16, 4);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.fillStyle = col;
      rr(x0, y, Math.max(1, (Math.abs(val) / scale) * bw), 16, 4);
      ctx.fill();
      label(eng(val, 'J', 2), x0 + bw - 8, y + 13, 0.75, 'right', 10);
    });
    const pct = Math.abs(wBatt) > 1e-18 ? (u / wBatt) * 100 : 0;
    label(`the capacitor keeps ${pct.toFixed(0)}%`, SIDE.x + SIDE.w / 2, top + 124, 0.6, 'center', 12, GREEN);
    label('the rest is heat on the way in', SIDE.x + SIDE.w / 2, top + 142, 0.4, 'center', 10);
  }

  // --- readouts --------------------------------------------------------------

  const el = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLElement;
  const setRow = (n: number, lab: string, val: string) => {
    el('l' + n).innerHTML = subHtml(lab);
    el('r' + n).textContent = val;
  };
  function updateReadout() {
    const q = cap() * v;
    setRow(1, 'Charge Q = CV', eng(q, 'C'));
    setRow(2, 'Voltage V_C', v.toFixed(3) + ' V');
    setRow(3, 'Current I = C dV/dt', eng(current(), 'A'));
    setRow(4, 'Capacitance C', eng(cap(), 'F'));
    if (state.src === 'ac') {
      const xc = 1 / (2 * Math.PI * freqHz() * cap());
      setRow(5, 'Reactance X_C', fmtR(xc));
      setRow(6, 'Frequency', eng(freqHz(), 'Hz', 1));
    } else {
      setRow(5, 'Time constant τ = RC', eng(tau(), 's'));
      setRow(6, 'Field E = V/d', eng(v / state.d, 'V/m'));
    }
    setRow(7, 'Energy ½CV²', eng(0.5 * cap() * v * v, 'J'));
  }

  // --- loop ------------------------------------------------------------------

  function draw() {
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    label('Capacitor', 20, 30, 0.85, 'left', 14);
    label(
      state.src === 'manual'
        ? 'drive the source yourself and watch the charge follow'
        : state.src === 'ac'
          ? 'the charge sloshes back and forth, and never crosses'
          : 'a battery, a switch, and a queue of electrons',
      20,
      52,
      0.5,
      'left',
      11,
      GREEN
    );
    const legend: [string, string][] = [
      [NEG, 'electron'],
      [POS, 'missing electron'],
      [WARM, 'field'],
    ];
    let x = W - 20;
    for (let k = legend.length - 1; k >= 0; k--) {
      const [c, tx] = legend[k];
      const tw = textWidth(tx, 11);
      label(tx, x, 30, 0.55, 'right', 11);
      ctx.fillStyle = c;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(x - tw - 11, 26, 5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      x -= tw + 32;
    }
    drawScene();
    drawScope();
    drawSide();
  }

  let last = performance.now();
  function frame(now: number) {
    let dt = (now - last) / 1000;
    last = now;
    dt = Math.min(0.05, Math.max(0, dt));
    for (let k = pops.length - 1; k >= 0; k--) {
      pops[k].life -= dt * 2.6;
      if (pops[k].life <= 0) pops.splice(k, 1);
    }
    if (state.running) {
      clock += dt;
      const qBefore = cap() * v;
      physics(dt);
      // The queue creeps forward by exactly the charge that moved, so the
      // electrons in the wire and the balls on the plates always agree.
      train += ((cap() * v - qBefore) / qBall()) * SPACING;
    }
    draw();
    updateReadout();
    requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  }

  // --- controls --------------------------------------------------------------

  const runBtn = el('run');
  runBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    state.running = !state.running;
    runBtn.textContent = state.running ? 'Pause' : 'Run';
  });
  el('reset').addEventListener('click', reset);

  let ready = false;
  function bindRange(id: string, apply: (n: number) => void, restart = false) {
    const inp = el(id) as HTMLInputElement;
    const run = () => {
      apply(+inp.value);
      if (restart && ready) reset();
    };
    inp.addEventListener('input', run);
    run();
  }
  bindRange('vs', (n) => {
    state.vs = n / 10;
    el('vsval').textContent = `${state.vs.toFixed(1)} V`;
  });
  bindRange('freq', (n) => {
    state.freq = n / 100;
    el('fval').textContent = eng(freqHz(), 'Hz', 1);
  });
  bindRange('r', (n) => {
    state.r = Math.round(100 * Math.pow(10, (n / 100) * 4));
    el('rval').textContent = fmtR(state.r);
  }, true);
  bindRange('a', (n) => {
    state.area = n / 100;
    el('aval').textContent = `${state.area.toFixed(2)} m²`;
  }, true);
  bindRange('d', (n) => {
    state.d = n * 1e-6;
    el('dval').textContent = `${n} µm`;
  }, true);
  bindRange('k', (n) => {
    state.kappa = n / 10;
    el('kval').textContent = state.kappa.toFixed(1);
  }, true);
  bindRange('rate', (n) => {
    state.rate = n / 100;
    el('rateval').textContent = `${state.rate.toFixed(1)}×`;
  });
  (el('lines') as HTMLInputElement).addEventListener('change', (e) => {
    state.lines = (e.target as HTMLInputElement).checked;
  });

  const show = (id: string, on: boolean) => {
    el(id).style.display = on ? '' : 'none';
  };
  function syncControls() {
    show('ctl-sw', state.src === 'dc');
    show('ctl-f', state.src === 'ac');
    el('vlab').textContent =
      state.src === 'manual' ? 'Drive it yourself' : state.src === 'ac' ? 'Amplitude' : 'Battery';
    el('vhint').textContent =
      state.src === 'manual' ? 'drag me up and down' : state.src === 'ac' ? 'peak volts' : 'battery volts';
    const inp = el('vs') as HTMLInputElement;
    inp.min = state.src === 'manual' ? '-120' : '0';
    if (state.src !== 'manual' && +inp.value <= 0) inp.value = '60';
    state.vs = +inp.value / 10;
    el('vsval').textContent = `${state.vs.toFixed(1)} V`;
    el('fval').textContent = eng(freqHz(), 'Hz', 1);
  }

  el('src').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    document.querySelectorAll('#src button').forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
    btn.classList.add('active');
    state.src = btn.dataset.s as 'manual' | 'dc' | 'ac';
    syncControls();
    reset();
  });
  el('mode').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    document.querySelectorAll('#mode button').forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
    btn.classList.add('active');
    state.mode = btn.dataset.m as 'charge' | 'discharge' | 'auto';
    phase = state.mode === 'discharge' ? 'discharge' : 'charge';
    t = 0;
  });

  syncControls();
  reset();
  ready = true;
  requestAnimationFrame(frame);
</script>

<style>
  .cp-canvas {
    touch-action: none;
  }
  .scale-hint {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    margin-top: 3px;
  }
  .check {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .check input {
    accent-color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
